WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:09.400
Hi, welcome back to the at-home retreat,

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.260
and thanks to Xiaoping for translating for me.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.600
We're at session 22,

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:27.620
and the name of this session is
"The Necessary Fire-fighting Equipment."

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:35.020
And it means there's a fire.
Here you see a picture of a house on fire.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:46.880
Actually, I have been in houses that caught on fire.
In the monastery, one house caught on fire.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:57.000
It's very frightening.
Once it gets up to a certain kind of temperature,

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:03.420
then it's very, very difficult to stop the fire.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.240
So let's read the text.

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:09.760
de tabuy tar du kyi lo kye ne
(DE LTA BU'I THAR 'DOD KYI BLO SKYES NA)

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:17.980
So let's say you finally got this Elon Musk inspiration,
"I'm going to get out of this trouble.

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:29.800
I want to find a cool life, not just this stupid life."

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.980
By the way, it doesn't mean you kill yourself, okay?

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:43.040
It means you make some cool adjustments,
and then life is like magic.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:52.500
So once you decide to get out of the jail,
lo kye na (BLO SKYES NA),
"once (you) make that decision"

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.920
tarpar drupay lam la lap gu
(THAR PAR BGROD PA'I LAM LA BSLAB DGOS)--

00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:06.560
you have to study or train yourself in
some kind of path for getting out of trouble.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:17.740
So we're moving on to
another great subject of the lam rim (LAM RIM).

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:26.340
If the last twenty-one videos were successful,

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:36.200
you ... and us, we've all been inspired to get out
of this place and to find a better place.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:46.100
Now we're going to need a path,
or instructions, on how to get out.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.799
tarpar drupay lam gyi rangshin ten la bappa
(THAR PAR BGROD PA'I LAM GYI RANG BZHIN GTAN LA DBAB PA)

00:02:52.820 --> 00:03:03.080
We're going to describe the path that you need to follow
to change your life completely and reach a cool life.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:13.500
shepa la nyi (BSHAD PA LA GNYIS)--
this "explanation is going to have two parts."

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:16.240
ten ji tabu shik gi korwa le dokpa dang
(RTEN JI LTA BU ZHIG GIS 'KHOR BA LAS LDOG PA DANG)

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:22.640
Well, what kind of ten (RTEN) are you going to need
to get out of this cycle of pain?

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:27.460
What kind of ten. ten means "body and mind."

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:39.260
So this is part of the discussion
of the equipment to put out the fire.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:47.040
Like in ballet,

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:51.060
in Russia,

00:03:52.380 --> 00:04:01.940
when they're going to... they actually measure children's legs when they're like six years old.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:12.420
And at the age of six, based on how long
their leg is compared to their chest--

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:21.140
they actually choose ballet dancers at that age
and start training them.

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:32.480
So they figured out what are the perfect proportions
to dance ballet successfully.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:46.820
So, what's the perfect body and mind
to dance your way out of the Wheel of Life?

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:55.760
And then once you get that equipment,

00:04:57.140 --> 00:04:59.720
that body and mind,

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:03.820
lam ji tabu shik gi korwa le dokpa
(LAM JI LTA BU ZHIG GIS 'KHOR BA LAS LDOG PA)--

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:11.920
then we're going to move on to another subject which is,
"what kind of path do you have to follow
to get out of this wheel?"

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:21.140
So today we're going to start with
describing the perfect body and mind.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:26.600
What's the perfect equipment?

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:30.940
dangpo ni, detar korway nye mik sam ne
(DANG PO NI, DE LTAR 'KHOR BA'I NYES DMIGS BSAMS NAS)

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:41.460
So give it a good thought--like we just took you through all this long part on how to realize you're in the jail.

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:55.660
Then you should think about
"what's the one quality that is typical of sansara?"

00:05:55.660 --> 00:06:02.920
If you had to describe sansara, the wheel of pain,
in one word, what word would you choose?

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.780
And it's this: nu chu kyi korwa (SNOD BCUD KYI 'KHOR BA)--

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:19.520
This circle of life, and whether you're talking
about "the world around us, or (you're talking about) the people who live in that world,"

00:06:20.140 --> 00:06:25.560
which in Tibetan is called the cup and the coffee.

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:37.280
The world is called the cup, and the coffee is the people in the world. The world is called the cup, and the people are all what is in the cup.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:51.600
So whether you're talking about the cup,
which is the whole outer world,

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:58.840
or you're talking about the coffee in the cup,
which is all the people who live in that world,

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:14.540
there's one quality that they share.
The outer world and the people living in the world,
there's one quality that they all share.

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:24.960
And it's a beautiful image.
It's called lung gi kyupay chunda (RLUNG GIS BSKYOD PA'I CHU ZLA)

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:26.820
say lung gi

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:28.940
kupay

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:30.520
chunda.

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:33.760
lung (RLUNG) here means "the wind."

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:38.540
kyupay (BSKYOD PA'I) means "moved by" the wind.

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:47.180
chu (CHU) means "the surface of the ocean," for example.

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:57.100
And nda (ZLA) means
"the reflection of the moon" on top of the ocean.

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:03.300
Then if you go out on the ocean at night--

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:10.880
I used to go out, my dad used to take us out for two or three days in the ocean for fishing,

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:19.780
and it's kind of frightening because
 he goes so far you cannot see the land anymore,

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:28.120
and you're in a small boat for two or three days,

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:39.620
and sometimes there's a full moon, and at night it's very, very beautiful. You watch the moon on the water.

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:46.980
Then if a little bit of wind comes,

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:54.740
then that image of the moon,
that reflection of the moon, is rippling like this.

00:08:57.440 --> 00:09:07.080
And it says here that's the one quality of the world and the people in the world which we both share.

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:11.800
Nothing stays the same,

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:15.540
even for a second.

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:23.120
Our whole life is constantly shifting
and the world around us is constantly shifting.

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:28.980
kechik kyang mi dupay jikpay mitakpa
(SKAD CIG KYANG MI SDOD PAR 'JIG PA'I MI RTAG PA)

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:37.100
Nothing stays more than a second.
Things are being destroyed moment by moment.

00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:43.060
So that's the one problem of our life.

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:49.480
korway de jor nam ni duk drul gyi deng kay dripma dang drawar
'KHOR BA'I BDE 'BYOR RNAMS NI DUG SBRUL GYI GDENGS KA'I GRIB MA DANG 'DRA BAR

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:58.240
This is a very powerful image, and it's a little bit difficult.
korwa ('KHOR BA) means "here in this cycle of pain."

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:09.860
de jor (BDE 'BYOR), dewa dang jorpa (BDE BA DANG 'BYOR PA)
means "any happiness we can find" or
any money or things we can find.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:18.600
They are like the... dripma (GRIB MA) means "the shadow,"

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:27.920
of the deng ka (GDENGS KA)--
means that special snake called a cobra. And they have this special hood, a little bit of a hood.

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:36.400
Of the duk drul (DUG SBRUL). duk drul means
"a very, very poisonous cobra snake."

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:48.120
nok chung la nyen che (MNOG CHUNG LA NYEN CHE).
nok chung (MNOG CHUNG) means "not really very important."

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:57.120
nyen che (NYEN CHE) means "actually a sign of great danger."

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:07.960
So don't think about the ...
and we had a similar snake in my three-year retreat.

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:14.480
Very poisonous. And they have a hood.

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:23.760
And if the sun shines,

00:11:24.360 --> 00:11:33.240
and you're looking at the ground and you see the shadow of this snake's head,

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:38.600
and you are like, "Oh! Such a beautiful shape.

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:44.260
Kind of a beautiful circle."

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:53.160
Maybe it looks beautiful. A little bit.

00:11:54.800 --> 00:12:02.700
But it's a shadow of a thing which is very, very close, which is highly poisonous.

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:17.240
So we are fascinated by "Oh, it's such a beautiful round shape--look how beautiful it is!"

00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:28.020
But it's really the shadow of the snake's hood,
and an extremely poisonous snake.

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:34.000
Okay, for one hundred dollars, Xiaoping--

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:42.500
What's the shadow metaphor? It's a metaphor for what?

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:47.900
[Xiaoping: The circle of samsara?]
No.

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:54.940
de jor. de jor. We just had it. Don't look. You got it Stanley? de jor?

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:58.140
Any happiness.

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:04.900
Any little happiness or any money
or things you can find in this life.

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:10.280
Don't get attached to it.

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:15.940
Don't get close to it and say, "Oh, so beautiful!"

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:24.780
It's just a shadow of the head
of a highly poisonous snake.

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:38.900
All the happiness you can find in this life,
and all the money and things you can find
in this life, have two qualities.

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:50.560
Number one: nok chung--completely unimportant.

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:55.860
Piece of shadow on the ground.

00:13:56.960 --> 00:14:03.060
And nyen chewa--at the same time, extremely dangerous.

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:07.400
It's a wonderful image.

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:12.780
Then he explains it a little bit.

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:15.800
drowa nga gang du kye kyang
('GRO BA LNGA GANG DU SKYES KYANG)

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:23.500
No matter which of the five parts
of this suffering wheel you are born into--

00:14:25.620 --> 00:14:35.540
and here they're talking about the traditional five divisions inside the twelve links in the Wheel of Life.

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:44.160
And there you can see animals, hungry spirits,

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:54.000
hell beings, humans, gods and demigods
counted as one together.

00:14:56.140 --> 00:15:00.300
Sometimes they are separated into six.

00:15:01.780 --> 00:15:11.420
It doesn't matter, these are the five choices where you can be born. There's no more. There is always just those five.

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:19.820
It's like five prison cells.

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:28.140
And it doesn't matter which one you go in,
you're still in the jail.

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:31.198
me barway kyim (ME 'BAR BA'I KHYIM)

00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:42.160
Each one of those five kinds of life form
is like a house which is on fire. Big fire.

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:54.160
No matter what life form you take,
you're still in a burning house.

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:08.240
tsun rar chupa (BTZON RAR CHUD PA) means "you are still in a cell," almost like you are in a cell inside a burning house.

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:18.900
ne de dak la mi du (GNAS DE DAG LA MI 'DOD)--
try to get over any attachment to this burning house.

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:23.780
tardu kye (THAR 'DOD SKYE)--

00:16:23.780 --> 00:16:26.240
try to think, "How can I get out?"

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:33.100
korwa le tardu kyi lo chu min kyepa na
('KHOR BA LAS THAR 'DOD KYI BLO BCOS MIN SKYES PA NA)

00:16:33.980 --> 00:16:41.860
If you are able to get a state of mind
where you want to escape from the wheel--

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:50.600
and there's an important word here called chu min (COS MIN).

00:16:51.580 --> 00:16:56.320
It's an abbreviation for chuma mayinpa (BCOS MA MA YIN PA)

00:16:56.800 --> 00:17:07.540
And it means a "genuine" wish and not just like a fake wish, like "Oh yeah, I wish I could get out, but..."

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:14.640
korway gyu tse chepa na
('KHOR BA'I RGYU RTZAD BCAD PA NA)--

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:22.820
if you really want to cut this wheel at its root,

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:32.420
le nyon nyi dang (LAS NYON GNYIS DANG)--
you're going to have to stop karma
and negative emotions.

00:17:35.040 --> 00:17:41.540
And you know, if somebody gave you a choice--
okay, I'll give you a choice.

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:52.180
This afternoon we can attack your bad karma
or we can attack your negative emotions.

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:57.440
Which would you choose?

00:17:58.940 --> 00:18:04.180
Negative emotions or the karma?
Which one to attack first?

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:05.740
[Xiaoping: negative emotions]

00:18:05.740 --> 00:18:08.520
Yeah, because they are the root. So, go for the root.

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:17.080
And if you could choose among all the negative emotions, if you could choose one to attack,

00:18:20.420 --> 00:18:25.440
what's the number one negative emotion in the kitchen?

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:33.720
"I didn't do anything!
He's yelling at me, I didn't do anything."

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:48.160
All the troublemakers in the whole world are in two big groups: negative emotions and karma.

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:51.960
Which group to attack first?

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:59.100
Negative emotions, because they make the karma,
so attack the negative emotions first.

00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:08.380
There's 84,000 negative emotions.
Which one do you want me to attack first?

00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:15.000
Attack your misunderstanding of your husband.
"I didn't do anything."

00:19:17.360 --> 00:19:19.520
de shompay tab la be gu
(DE GZHOM PA'I THABS LA 'BAD DGOS)

00:19:19.520 --> 00:19:24.420
You've got to work hard to kill that one.

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:33.480
de yang ten ni (DE YANG RTEN NI)--
Now what kind of body and mind are perfect for this fight?

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:45.900
delnjor tsang shing (DAL 'BYOR TSANG ZHING)--
well, first of all, do you have all
the spiritual leisures and fortunes?

00:19:47.260 --> 00:19:49.960
Were you born as a human?

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:53.580
Do you have a pretty healthy body?

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:57.980
Do you have fairly good intelligence?

00:19:58.660 --> 00:20:04.200
Do you live in a world where the Dharma even exists?

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:10.300
And we went through this list already.

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:19.860
Yeah, I have that. I mean it's my life's not perfect but I have enough food, I have a nice place to stay, I'm okay.

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:27.660
I have a fairly good life.

00:20:29.860 --> 00:20:39.440
tsang chu (TSANGS SPYOD) literally it means "someone who is keeping celibacy, who doesn't have sex."

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:45.540
By the way, the Sanskrit is brahmacharya.

00:20:47.860 --> 00:20:55.360
But it became a general word for all of us
who are trying to practice Buddhism.

00:20:58.720 --> 00:21:05.920
So we have food and shelter,
we live in a country where we can practice Buddhism,

00:21:12.180 --> 00:21:16.240
we live in a country where we can practice,

00:21:17.720 --> 00:21:24.380
and we actually have available to us
three important practices.

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:36.080
hlakpar tsultrim kyi lappa (LHAG PAR TSUL KHRIMS KYI BSLAB PA),
hlakpar ting ngen dzin gyi lappa (LHAG PAR TING NGE 'DZIN GYI BSLAB PA),
hlakpar sherab kyi lappa (LHAG PAR SHES RAB KYI BSLAB PA)

00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:39.700
These are called the three trainings.

00:21:40.460 --> 00:21:47.280
What are they? And they're called the
"three special trainings" in Buddhism.

00:21:48.380 --> 00:21:55.300
I have heard about the training of good behaviour
that doesn't hurt other people.

00:21:58.940 --> 00:22:07.180
Even in these lam rim videos
they are teaching me concentration or meditation.

00:22:11.340 --> 00:22:17.520
And I have heard teachings about emptiness,
especially in the kitchen.

00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:35.480
So my human body is not just a normal human body.
I have a really special human body. I have food.
I have a house. I have Buddhism.
I have those three trainings.

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:52.100
So really this is now the exact time
when I should be getting another wheel.
I have everything. Everything's ready.

00:22:56.700 --> 00:23:02.840
And then Geshe Potowa,
who lived exactly a thousand years ago--

00:23:03.600 --> 00:23:07.280
and I have his picture here from a thangka (THANG KA),

00:23:09.100 --> 00:23:12.560
with two other Kadampa (BKA GDAMS PA) masters.

00:23:14.840 --> 00:23:19.320
He said ngar de tsam shik kyampa la (SNGAR DE TZAM ZHIG 'KHYAMS PA LA),

00:23:19.660 --> 00:23:26.920
"I've been wandering through this wheel of pain for many lifetimes"

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:29.920
rank lok ma jung tsa na (RANG LOG MA BYUNG TZA NA)--

00:23:29.920 --> 00:23:42.640
And you know what? The wheel... "up to now in countless lifetimes, the wheel never cooperated with me and stopped by itself." And I didn't do anything, it--

00:23:42.640 --> 00:23:48.620
that wheel is not going to stop by itself.
It didn't stop by itself for billions of years.

00:23:51.880 --> 00:23:55.420
da yang rang lok mi-ongwe
(DA YANG RANG LOG MI 'ONG BAS)

00:23:55.440 --> 00:24:02.680
"And probably it's not going to stop
on its own in the future, from now."

00:24:06.120 --> 00:24:12.540
Therefore, dok go (BZLOG DGO)--
maybe "I have to stop it."

00:24:13.900 --> 00:24:17.860
Well, when should I start stopping it?

00:24:19.800 --> 00:24:23.080
du kyang da re (DUS KYANG DA RES)--
Start now!

00:24:23.660 --> 00:24:31.160
Why? delnjor toppay du (DAL 'BYOR THOB PA'I DUS)--
"You've got all those perfect circumstances."

00:24:32.660 --> 00:24:34.840
You're not too old.

00:24:34.900 --> 00:24:37.440
You have food. You have a house.

00:24:38.380 --> 00:24:46.520
You heard about Buddhism.
People taught you about morality:
not hurting other people.

00:24:48.400 --> 00:24:50.400
People taught you meditation.

00:24:51.440 --> 00:24:53.800
People taught you about emptiness.

00:24:55.240 --> 00:24:57.660
The time is now.

00:24:58.640 --> 00:25:02.540
dir yin she sungpa tar lu ten di nyi le hlakpa me la
('DIR YIN ZHES GSUNGS PA LTAR LUS RTEN
'DI NYID LAS LHAG PA MED LA)--

00:25:02.740 --> 00:25:08.500
"You are never going to get a better chance" than today.

00:25:12.260 --> 00:25:16.700
You have the equipment you need to put the fire out.

00:25:18.900 --> 00:25:23.660
Actually, it couldn't be more perfect
than what you have now.

00:25:25.020 --> 00:25:28.700
"Oh no, Geshe-la, there is a virus now!"

00:25:29.680 --> 00:25:37.340
No. Good body, good home, lots of Buddhism,
and a virus. That's perfect!

00:25:40.780 --> 00:25:47.660
Maybe you get scared a little bit.
Maybe you start to think about where you're going next.

00:25:48.920 --> 00:25:54.940
So to have all of those things plus the virus--
you're super lucky today.

00:25:59.100 --> 00:26:08.360
In America in the last three weeks,
every American became half Buddhist suddenly.

00:26:13.440 --> 00:26:19.000
I don't mean they all say,
"Oh, I want to try Buddhism."
They didn't say that.

00:26:20.880 --> 00:26:29.100
But they're all talking all day about only one thing.
"Oh, what about the virus? What can we do?
How do we get out of this?"

00:26:32.200 --> 00:26:38.800
So from that point of view, they all became half Buddhist--they want to get out of this trouble.

00:26:45.660 --> 00:26:49.160
We have perfect circumstances.

00:26:50.760 --> 00:26:55.580
Good body--not perfect, but okay, it works.

00:26:57.200 --> 00:27:00.920
And a mind, it's not perfect, but okay, it works.

00:27:01.800 --> 00:27:08.940
And you know we heard a lot of lam rim.
thirty-four retreats already, for ten years.

00:27:14.080 --> 00:27:17.300
So if you want to stop that wheel,

00:27:19.180 --> 00:27:22.500
start this month.

00:27:23.340 --> 00:27:24.820
Perfect.

00:27:25.420 --> 00:27:27.920
Okay, how to stop the wheel?

00:27:28.940 --> 00:27:31.540
We need three things.

00:27:32.060 --> 00:27:38.500
And we're going to learn about those
tomorrow in session 23.

00:27:39.560 --> 00:27:43.220
Thank you again Xiaoping for translating.

